<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Middle East live: South Korea prepares for military deployment in Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d25797fb64c30d537eee046dc63135a9eb719256d23536d1be8cbe5c1bc51f9</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T02:56:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-middle-east-live-south-korea-prepares-for-military-deployment-in-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">South Korea is considering sending military assets to the Strait of Hormuz to support freedom of navigation, media reported Thursday, though Seoul denied it had decided on a deployment. Iran launched strikes on American military targets in the Gulf, in retaliation for an attack that killed four people at a wedding on Tuesday night. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>OpenAI begins rollout of GPT-6 with focus on cyber security safeguards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:beeeacb11c87ad142115887411e9ae1620b881090ff4baf5f6b71d1acb4656f8</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T02:44:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260904-openai-begins-rollout-of-gpt-6-with-focus-on-cyber-security-safeguards" /><summary type="html">OpenAI said Thursday it would begin rolling out GPT-6, its most powerful AI model yet, to select customers, touting stronger safety safeguards as concerns grow over the cybersecurity risks posed by increasingly capable artificial intelligence systems.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen to cut another 50,000 jobs to counter tariffs and Chinese competition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f21b0af9bb4067b65c1871d394bb6502df5156ab86126c0fd5c7a0a690eee2e</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T00:34:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260904-volkswagen-to-cut-another-50-000-jobs-to-counter-tariffs-and-chinese-competition" /><summary type="html">Volkswagen announced Thursday that it will cut another 50,000 jobs worldwide under its biggest restructuring in the company's 89-year history, as the German carmaker faces pressure from US tariffs, overcapacity and fierce competition from Chinese rivals. The plan also sets out the future of four German plants.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia court upholds prison sentences of up to 45 years for opposition figures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faf972528262dbceecf70f11681a9c8a9b17bb25f08adf4effd50bbbe3d8eb72</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T22:17:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260903-tunisia-court-upholds-prison-sentences-of-up-to-45-years-for-opposition-figures" /><summary type="html">Tunisia's top court on Thursday upheld prison sentences of up to 45 years for opposition leaders, lawyers and businessmen convicted in a major conspiracy case, in a ruling opponents said further entrenches President Kais Saied's authoritarian rule.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia to buy Hugging Face for $12.93 billion in major AI expansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e018cc7042842cceb3ab94d2cfa62dacf6323448f943388e5b7ea21bb69844fb</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T21:34:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260903-nvidia-to-buy-hugging-face-for-12-93-billion-in-major-ai-expansion" /><summary type="html">Nvidia said Thursday it will buy AI developer platform Hugging Face for $12.93 billion, its latest major investment to expand its influence in open-source artificial intelligence. The deal would bring Nvidia closer to developers and broaden its customer base as tech giants develop chips to reduce reliance on the company.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>'50% savvy political tactics, 50% extraordinarily good luck' - the formula to Meloni's success?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23e8861208d2eb9229e21d86c3d020ff1d9db93c4243cf0bea3b4966bef85778</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T20:57:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260903-50-savvy-political-tactics-50-extraordinarily-good-luck-the-formula-to-meloni-s-success" /><summary type="html">Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government on Friday becomes the longest-lasting in Italy's postwar history -- a notable record that belies considerable challenges ahead of elections next year. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Nathalie Tocci, Director of the Istituto Affari Internazionali in Rome and Professor of Practice at the John Hopkins University SAIS. She says that Meloni's success comes down to "50 percent savvy political tactics and 50 percent extraordinarily good luck".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Shady surgeons and Nigeria organ harvesting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8f690c48bec2b3bc6ae2164cf5864d293af058ef5a77e57c8209118e1e26edd</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T20:15:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/shady-surgeons-and-nigeria-organ-harvesting" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, legal loopholes and gaps about specialised medicine may be driving Illegal organ harvesting in Nigeria. Also, South Sudan may be moving closer to delivering on elections scheduled for December. And on the islands of São Tomé and Príncipe, six colonial era plantation estates have just been added to the UNESCO World Heritage List.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>El Niño weather phenomenon set to deliver massive blow to global economy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99bc6a71ae627cee1f51b4a0853326b4537f722ced4b4215f1abcd49cc55246c</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T19:52:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260903-el-ni%C3%B1o-weather-phenomenon-set-to-deliver-massive-blow-to-global-economy" /><summary type="html">The UN warns El Niño is a "supersized" phenomenon that will hit the global economy. UK cider producers are feeling the impact of  drought. Plus, Nvidia buys Hugging Face for $12.9 billion.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>No, UN chief Guterres did not call Francesca Albanese 'out of control'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c98835e07f261ca025e070bf1dd36802d923f7d0c85cbb5bd1e9b4900845a6fb</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T19:34:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260903-no-un-chief-guterres-did-not-call-francesca-albanese-out-of-control" /><summary type="html">Pro-Israel lobby group UN Watch alleged that Secretary-General Antonio Guterres referred Francesca Albanese, the UN’s Special Rapporteur on Palestine, "out of control", saying he'd previously called her a "horrible woman." But Guterres named no one in his remarks. He said “many” independent rapporteurs were “totally out of control,” without singling out any individual. The UN has since said linking the comment specifically to Albanese is a “misreading” of his remarks. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Deadlocked jury in Lindsay Clancy's children murder trial deliberates for sixth day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:646ada031df19be906de510cfb69ee36507a8c367d0bf2d4cfbfa2911f89a0db</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T18:44:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/deadlocked-jury-in-lindsay-clancy-s-children-murder-trial-deliberates-for-sixth-day--4c827f35230b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/deadlocked-jury-in-lindsay-clancy-s-children-murder-trial-deliberates-for-sixth-day" /><summary type="html">Jurors in the Lindsay Clancy murder trial are deliberating for a sixth day in Plymouth, Massachusetts after twice saying they can’t agree whether the former labor and delivery nurse is criminally responsible for killing her three young children. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Fight through darkness, water’: Nepal survivor recounts escape from flood-hit tunnel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccc7922370362030023b46f17c3b4f15c5887b9bd06182d3d44548095e7ed085</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:22:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel--029aa5abd2d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel" /><summary type="html">A Nepalese worker recounts his harrowing escape from a hydropower project tunnel after last week's devastating flood. Around 900 workers remain trapped in tunnels at six hydroelectric plants in Nepal as the number of missing in the Himalayan disaster rose to 5,624 on Thursday, according to Nepalese and Chinese authorities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Anti-Christian murder in Syria? No indication he was killed because of his faith</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38eb3596fe7025786ac960d1b86b0b44e84cf4f0d854f75e600b8a110328577d</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:00:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith--cf972620ce2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith" /><summary type="html">A Christian man by the name of Nader Boulos Tannous was murdered in Homs, Syria on August 15, 2026. After his death, Israel, Greece and Cyprus were quick to denounce what they called an anti-Christian act. Several days later however, authorities in Homs said the suspect had admitted killing Tannous as part of a personal dispute going back to 2012.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>WMO chief says El Nino could be strongest in four decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:658c5afd55c56eda14a34be8d43dae796b5125462de5ad1e6b940e6f033faf54</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:11:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-wmo-chief-says-el-nino-could-be-strongest-in-four-decades--061486528cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-wmo-chief-says-el-nino-could-be-strongest-in-four-decades" /><summary type="html">El Nino could be the strongest since records began four decades ago, the United Nations' climate agency warned Thursday, with the UN chief warning the world is in the "danger zone of extreme weather". The naturally-occurring weather phenomenon is set to become "very strong" in the months ahead and is near certain to persist through to February, the World Meteorological Organization (WMO) said. FRANCE 24's Journalist Carys Garland tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two Palestinian teens killed in West Bank raid by Israeli settlers and army</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a34fe30a75d20113361d08532594f1b53b54cc5e237b17eea855d7bed0257978</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:09:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-two-palestinian-teens-killed-in-west-bank-raid-by-israeli-settlers-and-army--9187488fdbab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-two-palestinian-teens-killed-in-west-bank-raid-by-israeli-settlers-and-army" /><summary type="html">Two Palestinian teenagers ⁠were killed on ​Wednesday in an attack by Israeli settler militants and ​army troops on their village in the occupied West Bank, local officials and the Palestinian health ministry said, amid an uptick in violence ​by ‌Jewish settlers in the territory. The Israeli military said in a statement its forces had entered al-Mughayyir to ​provide security for police officers and an Israeli ‌civilian seeking to retrieve livestock.</summary></entry><entry><title>US energy firms dominate Venezuela deals worth billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ec4d9d56936dbfd95c8e8e7796ee57000d09641fc672468c80fdb4cb4334317</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:06:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-energy-firms-dominate-venezuela-deals-worth-billions--d1c9283e2081.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-energy-firms-dominate-venezuela-deals-worth-billions" /><summary type="html">US energy firms on Wednesday signed a raft of multi-billion-dollar deals with Venezuela, days after the South American country agreed to grant the United States control of a huge chunk of its vast oil reserves. President Donald Trump has talked up the agreement on Venezuela's oil reserves as the "biggest oil deal in world history." But the deals have raised major questions about Venezuela's sovereignty, as FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>France agriculture production sees economic hit from heatwaves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e898af149e954bd9add039e176a098b7363a6eb84cf3eb2e6a94ab5ca0eba63d</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:05:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-agriculture-production-sees-economic-hit-from-heatwaves--a5510b56d96e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-agriculture-production-sees-economic-hit-from-heatwaves" /><summary type="html">France's recent heatwaves didn't just pose enormous health risks, they also hampered the economy. Authorities have estimated that the recent heat and drought caused production to plummet and expect wealth generated by the agricultural sector to decline by 8% over the course of the year. The knock-on effects will cost the French economy an estimated 0.1 percentage points of growth in 2026.</summary></entry><entry><title>US feminist icon and journalist Gloria Steinem dies aged 92</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:362299c42f7d15ae80cb26d32cb18cd49d51c87a8827f1355a0b54201f13876c</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:39:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-feminist-icon-and-journalist-gloria-steinem-dies-aged-92--49355b9195f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-feminist-icon-and-journalist-gloria-steinem-dies-aged-92" /><summary type="html">The co-founder of Ms. Magazine and celebrated feminist icon Gloria Steinem has died at her home at the age of 92. An internationally recognised activist in the fight for women's equality, she spoke out for the legalisation of abortion, same-sex marriage, and equal pay. She began her journalism career in New York in the 1960s. Politically, she was an outspoken critic of Donald Trump, arguing that the US had taken many steps back when it came to women's rights. FRANCE 24's Journalist and host of "The 51%" tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine’s drained Kakhovka Dam is strategic for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b75535ba5b2e3b40864dc95cec2a68aaade9d7c558fdd5c1b4ac26f552fd4d2f</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia--143f379d846d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia" /><summary type="html">Small groups of Russian soldiers have been inching forward through the vast, drained Kakhovka reservoir since they blew up the dam in June 2023. Russian forces are infiltrating this “no man’s land” for reconnaissance purposes rather than for a future military offensive, said a military expert.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Giorgia Meloni government becomes Italy's longest-lasting since World War II</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb288a628352b3125b69aaa93eaaac4f7b7e219885bcbd67b44e4eb98525e145</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii--f321ed0a24d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii" /><summary type="html">Italy's first female Prime Minister, Giorgia Meloni, has surpassed a longevity record set by the late Silvio Berlusconi. When she took office in 2022, many European allies viewed her with unease, given her party's neo-fascist roots. Yet she has governed pragmatically, working within EU institutions and even supporting Ukraine. Domestically, however, she has targeted same-sex parents and clamped down on press freedom.</summary></entry><entry><title>France-UK ties and humour celebrated as London receives Bayeux Tapestry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4f28fcafbce4d727dccf31cadd35d6f3c5887ff42527d509fd46f5f395c28cb</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:27:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1--6ef2090555dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-uk-ties-and-humour-celebrated-as-london-receives-bayeux-tapestry-1" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel #Macron is in #London on the occasion of the #Bayeux Tapestry's exhibition at the #BritishMuseum. The 1,000-year-old work of woven art recounts the Battle of #Hastings, in which William the Conqueror – #KingCharles's ancestor – led the Norman Conquest of #England. An opportunity for the French president, the British PM Andy #Burnham and British monarch to celebrate the strong ties between the two countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>Driverless robotaxis hit the streets of London</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efec253a90027fce096ebcfe9e41caa1552e9e6bfec4d3ff4989f16ae79cbe21</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london--2660dfa1427c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-driverless-robotaxis-hit-the-streets-of-london" /><summary type="html">London is entering the era of autonomous vehicles: driverless cabs are now available through Uber and British tech firm Wayve in the capital. It marks a setback for Google's Waymo and Chinese giant Baidu, which have been eyeing Europe as a largely untapped market for autonomous vehicles. But for Wayve, it is its first mass-market rollout, and the company now plans to expand to Tokyo and 10 other cities with Uber.</summary></entry><entry><title>Murder of Daphne Caruana Galizia: Campaigner 'devastated' at tycoon's acquittal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afe1f013db35ec073f82243c21cac55cba688bcc63c3eff339ddab8709175ad5</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists--f0de620fc0ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/i-m-devastated-by-the-verdict-says-tom-gibson-deputy-dir-for-committee-to-protect-journalists" /><summary type="html">A campaigner who has worked on the case of murdered Maltese journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia since she was killed by a car bomb in 2017 has spoken of his devastation at the not guilty verdict.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez says no evidence Morocco orchestrated Ceuta border surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8380608a428d22b40240e0246814f5517989a3fc980959047e6e9d72b54f7e28</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:44:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:10:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-evidence-morocco-orchestrated-ceuta-border-surge--2deeeb297365.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-evidence-morocco-orchestrated-ceuta-border-surge" /><summary type="html">Spain has found no evidence to conclude that July's deadly border rush from Morocco into its enclave of Ceuta was orchestrated by Moroccan authorities, ​Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez ‌said on Thursday, countering allegations in a Spanish police report. Speaking in parliament, Sanchez responded to claims in ⁠the report that emerged this week suggesting the entry of over 70,000 people into Ceuta was not a spontaneous migration but a planned effort to overwhelm  border controls.</summary></entry></feed>
